\p{Differences from Init: cedar shares 23 of its 30 hottest static heads and 82 of its 100 with Init; the non-Init entries of its top 100 are \code{\verb~|Cedar.Thm.InstanceOfType~}, \code{\verb~|Std.DTreeMap.Internal.Impl.inner~}, \code{\verb~|Cedar.SymCC.Term.WellFormed~}, \code{\verb~|Cedar.Data.Map.find?~}, \code{\verb~|Cedar.Thm.Residual.WellTyped~}, \code{\verb~|Cedar.Validation.typeOf~} (type formers and plain definitions, no matcher or recursor). con-leche differs most among the non-Mathlib corpora (16 of 30 shared; \code{\verb~|PSum.inr~} 5.0\%, \code{\verb~|PSigma.mk~} 1.7\%, \code{\verb~|List.filter.match_1~} 1.2\%, \code{\verb~|ConLeche.Semantics.interp~} 0.9\%): its proofs carry packed mutual/well-founded arguments. The Mathlib corpora replace the equality lemmas by projections of the algebraic hierarchy (\code{\verb~|HMul.hMul~} 7.6\% on NSE, \code{\verb~|DFunLike.coe~} 2.3\% on mathlib).}

