\p{Proof sizes (expression records first written for the declaration): theorem median 31-71 nodes in every corpus, p99 984 (reachability) to 7,493 (con-leche), maximum 26 k (init), 86 k (cedar), 373 k (con-leche), 641 k (NSE), 92 k (mathlib); the largest 100 declarations hold 12.7\% of cedar's nodes, 22.7\% of con-leche's, 2.6\% of mathlib's. \strong{93-95\% of all expression nodes are private to one declaration} in every corpus (never referenced by a record of a later declaration; theorem segments 94-96\%, definition segments 89-92\%), which confirms ISA decision 3 (run-once terms are walked, not elaborated) on every corpus. Declarations whose \code{\verb~|(type, value)~} ids equal an earlier declaration's (private copies such as \code{\verb~|_sparseCasesOn_N~}): 15,042 on cedar = 1.26\% of its checking instructions, 0.06-1.0\% elsewhere.}
}

