}

\p{Reading for RLVM: the first line is what elaborated code replaces (operands in registers instead of a DAG walk with environment lookups); the second and third are what no tier removes while every value is interned. Inside the reduction phase of cedar (25.0\%): walking 11.6\%, construction 8.3\%, control 2.6\%, templates 1.1\%. Inside inference (42.2\%): inference proper 17.6\%, walking 12.9\% (evaluation of arguments and instantiation of Pi codomains, i.e. the \code{\verb~|TELE~} work), construction 8.7\%.}
}

\subtree{
\title{3.2 The corpora contain their libraries: the project's own declarations}

\table{
