}

\p{Three independent implementations agree: a library corpus needs one delta step per 200-600 bytes of export and 5-20 times as many inference and conversion events (cedar delta: rpylean 1.55 M, gruszka 2.17 M, nano-lean 2.77 M + 0.69 M firings). rpylean's iota is concentrated like nano-lean's (cedar: \code{\verb~|List.rec~} 946k, \code{\verb~|Int.rec~} 517k, \code{\verb~|Bool.rec~} 249k, \code{\verb~|Option.rec~} 216k, \code{\verb~|Nat.rec~} 181k; top 10 recursors = 91.7\%); its hottest delta entry is a type-level wrapper (\code{\verb~|outParam~}, 59.5k on cedar, 630k on mathlib): telescopes run trivial bodies too.}
}
}

